"The equitable semialgebraic regularity conjecture — MathDB (https://mathdb.com/p/364139/the-equitable-semialgebraic-regularity-conjecture)\nciteturn6search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; The equitable semialgebraic regularity conjecture\n\nThe equitable semialgebraic regularity conjecture\n\nConjecture open\n\nLet $H$H be a $k$k-partite semialgebraic hypergraph in $\\mathbb{R}^d$R d with total degree $D$D, and let $\\varepsilon>0$ε>0. An equitable partition is a partition of each vertex part into parts of equal size, with the regularity properties asserted by the equitable semialgebraic regularity lemma.\n\nEquitable regularity conjecture. The equitable semialgebraic regularity lemma holds with partitions into\n\n$$O_{d,k}\\left((D/\\varepsilon)^d\\right)$$O d,k​((D/ε)d)\n\nparts.\n\nThe proved regularity lemma has a loss in the dependence on $\\varepsilon$ε when passing to equitable partitions. The conjecture asks whether that loss can be removed in every dimension; the source notes that this is possible by a direct argument in dimension $d=1$d=1.\n\n## Progress summary\n\nRefresh\n\nNothing recorded yet. Refresh searches the literature and the public web for attempts on this problem, and writes the first summary here.\n\nsource: Jonathan Tidor and Hung-Hsun Hans Yu, “Multilevel polynomial partitioning and semialgebraic hypergraphs: regularity, Turán, and Zarankiewicz results”, arXiv:2407.20221 (2024).\n\nhypergraph-regularitysemialgebraic-geometry\n\n0\n\nposted by arXiv 5 days ago\n\n## 0 Replies\n\n* * *\n\nSign in to reply.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInder J. Taneja (https://rgmia.org/papers/v19/v19a163.pdf)\nciteturn6search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; 363595 = ((3 −6 + 3)!\nInder J. Taneja\nRGMIA Research Report Collection, 19(2016), pp.1-42, http://rgmia.org/v19.php\n362998 = 3! + (−6 + 2 + 9)! + 9! −8\n= −8 + 9! + (9 + 2 −6)! + 3!.\n363576 = 3!! + (6 + 3)! −(5 −7 + 6)!\n= 6! −