mples to Mubayi's supersaturation conjecture for every $k\\ge2$. The ratio $h_F(n,q)/(q c(n,F))$ tends to zero over ranges extending be… ▽ More For a fixed $k$-graph $F$, let $h_F(n,q)$ be the minimum number of copies of $F$ in an $n$-vertex $k$-graph with $\\text{ex}(n,F)+q$ edges. Let $c(n,F)$ be the minimum number created by adding one edge to an extremal $F$-free $k$-graph. We construct stable counterexamples to Mubayi's supersaturation conjecture for every $k\\ge2$. The ratio $h_F(n,q)/(q c(n,F))$ tends to zero over ranges extending beyond $n^{k-1}$. For graphs, we give examples of every chromatic number at least three. In particular, there is a graph $F$ for which this ratio tends to zero for $1\\le q=o(n^{4/3})$. For $k\\ge3$, we use connected linear expansions of $G=(M_a\\cup K_{1,b}\\cup I_h)\\vee K_{m_1,\\ldots,m_{k-1}}$. Under explicit parameter conditions, the ratio tends to zero for $1\\le q=o(n^{k-1+(b-1)/(a+b-1)})$ when $b\\ge k+1$. We prove the exact Turán theorems for both constructions and determine their unique extremal graphs and hypergraphs. Keywords: supersaturation; extremal graph; linear hypergraph; graph expansion; stability. △ Less\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMicro-Market Recovery Program - Violations and Inspections (https://data.cityofchicago.org/api/views/ujwc-724r/rows.pdf?app_token=U29jcmF0YS0td2VraWNrYXNz0)\nciteturn6search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9 months ago; 363595\nMicro-Market Recovery Program - Violations and Inspections\n499004\n21021\n(41.74591414289424, -87.6044070683873)\n137485\n93536\n(41.92030164790471, -87.74635064167563)\n498779\n25167\n(41.7492204442261, -87.60284636654364)\n77724\n39993\n(41.89273353570488, -87.71120650716249)\n428487\n363595\n(41.78257720306255, -87.64714334986937)\n428487\n363595\n(41.78257720306255, -87.64714334986937)\n428487\n363595\n(41.78257720306255, -87.64714334986937)\n498779\n25167\n(41.7492204442261, -87.60284636654364)\nPage 